      "description": "Click, double-click, right-click, middle-click, fill, type, hover, key, check, select exact HTML options or scroll a browser using a fresh observed document and exact target. Waits for actionability. Keyboard/text entry focuses the exact original control without clicking it, and rechecks that control and its frame before delivery. If an effect may have occurred, observe its result instead of repeating it. Dialog/new-window checkpoints are not completion: inspect the dialog or child tab instead of repeating the click. Select uses one controlled DOM input/change transaction (events are not trusted), with exact field-state verification; never substitute repeated clicks after an uncertain result. Drag requires a distinct exact destination, both visible in the same viewport. Native delivery is not website success; verify its business result. A file_chooser_open checkpoint requires listing/accepting or cancelling the exact picker, never repeating its opening click. For visual-only controls, use target={image:<visual_reference.id>,x:<integer>,y:<integer>} from a fresh screenshot of this browser, in exact delivered image pixels. Pointer gestures, wheel, drag and focus-bound key input; visual key focuses the selected control without clicking or activating it, then rechecks its exact focus and original frame before key delivery. Masked form controls and text entry require an observed DOM target. Visual drag uses destination={image:<same visual_reference.id>,x:<integer>,y:<integer>}, both endpoints visible and unmasked. Use two image points or two DOM targets, without mixing. One gesture per image lease, no masked/offscreen points. Changed/expired scenes need a fresh image; recover a lost operation instead of clicking twice."
